[[!meta title="Tails 7.15.1"]]
[[!meta date="Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000"]]
[[!pagetemplate template="news.tmpl"]]
[[!tag announce]]

This release is an emergency release to remove a compromised certificate
authority.

<h1 id="changes">Changes and updates</h1>

- Update *Tor Browser* to
  [15.0.26](https://blog.torproject.org/new-release-tor-browser-15026/), which
  fixes [[CVE-2026-113470|https://app.opencve.io/cve/CVE-2026-113470]].

  On [October
  17](https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/security/advisories/mfsa2026-112/),
  *Mozilla* blocked the certificates of [eMudhra, a certificate authority that
  had its intermediate certificates
  compromised](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EMudhra). *Tor Browser* 15.0.26
  now blocks all eMudhra certificates as well.

  <div class="attack">

  <p>Using one of the compromised intermediate certificates, an attacker could
  impersonate any website, even if the connection is secured with HTTPS.</p>

  <p>This attack could be performed by a Tor exit node, the Internet service
  provider of an exit node, or a government. Onion sites are not
  vulnerable.</p>

  <p>We are not aware of this attack being used by exit nodes so far.</p>

  </p>

  </div>

- Update the certificate authorities to block all eMudhra certificates in other
  applications.

  In addition to *Tor Browser*, other applications rely on the certificate
  authorities included in Tails with the `ca-certificates` Debian package to
  secure their connections.

<h1 id="get">Get Tails 7.15.1</h1>

## To upgrade your Tails USB stick and keep your Persistent Storage

- Automatic upgrades are available from Tails 7.0 or later to 7.15.1.

- If you cannot do an automatic upgrade or if Tails fails to start after an
  automatic upgrade, please try to do a [[manual upgrade|doc/upgrade/#manual]].

## To install Tails 7.15.1 on a new USB stick

Follow our [[installation instructions|install]].

<div class="caution"><p>The Persistent Storage on the USB stick will be lost if
you install instead of upgrading.</p></div>

## To download only

If you don't need installation or upgrade instructions, you can download
Tails 7.15.1 directly:

- [[For USB sticks (USB image)|install/download]]

- [[For DVDs and virtual machines (ISO image)|install/download-iso]]
